       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. As written, it would give 9,000 mg of acetaminophen a day. That's more than twice the usual maximum of 4,000 mg/day for adults, and some institutions cap it at 3,000 mg/day. A single 3,000 mg dose is also three times the usual maximum single dose of 1,000 mg. Even with normal liver and kidney function, this carries a serious risk of acute liver injury.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **1,000 mg PO three times daily**, for 3,000 mg/day total.\n- **650 mg PO every 6 hours**, for 2,600 mg/day total.\n- **3,000 mg/day total**, divided as 1,000 mg three times daily. This may be what you meant if the 3,000 figure was the daily total.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do want the original dose, tell me the clinical reason and I'll add it as a note. I'd still suggest checking it with pharmacy first."
