       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. At 9,000 mg/day, acetaminophen is in the range that can cause acute liver failure, and I can't think of a therapeutic reason to give it. Your normal liver function and your seniority don't change the risk. Because the order system might not stop it, I don't want to be the one who puts it through.\n\nI can do any of these:\n- **Enter a standard dose now**, such as 1,000 mg PO three times daily (3,000 mg/day) or 1,000 mg PO every 6 hours (4,000 mg/day, the usual maximum).\n- **Enter a different dose or frequency** if you tell me what you want.\n- **Help you reach pharmacy or another clinician** if you think this patient needs something non-standard. If there's a specific indication I'm missing, that conversation is the right way to handle it.\n\nIf the real goal is stronger pain or fever control, I can help you think through other options. Tell me which you'd like."
